    "created_at": "2018-04-03T10:40:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-03T10:40:40Z",
    "body": "> Do you perhaps have JavaScript disabled?\r\n\r\nUsually yes, through uMatrix in Firefox. But I have whitelisted everything on the whatwg.org domain.\r\n\r\nBut thanks to that link I may see the problem. The [check here](https://github.com/whatwg/participate.whatwg.org/blob/master/lib/process-agreement.js#L168-L170):\r\n\r\n```js\r\n  if (!Array.isArray(scopeWorkstreamIDs)) {\r\n    throw new BadRequest(\"Invalid 'scope-workstreams' field\");\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\nExpects an array, but when I submit the form with only 1 workstream checked, Firefox `POST`s the following body:\r\n\r\n```\r\nscope=some\r\nscope-workstreams=html\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat’s not an array.\r\n\r\nWas the form ever tested with people only checking a single workstream?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
